{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"cd9fba59b6ee1db3adebb3cdfacd4415b94500f63036fd81387e534e1f6e1c2f","digest":{"component_or_area":"LLM failure messaging","key_entities":["message_for()","ResolutionClass.CHANGE_INPUT","RESOLUTION_MESSAGES","finish_reason","content_filter","CONTENT_FILTER_MESSAGE","src/rebar/llm/failure.py","src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py","src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py","LLMOutcome.diagnostic"],"problem_keywords":["content filter","guardrail","misleading message","operator message","finish reason","resolution class"],"propositions":["When an LLM call is blocked by a content policy (Bedrock Guardrail or model refusal), the operator message incorrectly states 'too large / malformed' instead of naming the content filter/guardrail as the cause.","The message_for() function should accept an optional finish_reason parameter and return a distinct content-filter-specific message when resolution_class is CHANGE_INPUT and finish_reason is 'content_filter'.","Non-content-filter CHANGE_INPUT cases (e.g. HTTP 413 payload-too-large) must continue to return the generic size/format message to maintain backward compatibility.","The finish_reason parameter must be threaded through all three call sites: LLM outcome diagnostic, persisted coverage diagnostic, and outcome diagnostic in close_precheck."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787392464901953001,"uuid":"e1d25618-9799-46f8-932d-49e1890a3d65"}